  "capturedBaseStats": {
    "note": "What Frontier's own captures say about the base values in `data/ships/modules-*.jsonc`, joined through the library's own journal-label→field mapping rather than a hand-written one. This reaches fields the in-game audit could not — a hardpoint's reserve ammo, projectile speed, the shield-generator and booster resistances, an armour module's hull boost — because a `Loadout` states every engineered module's unmodified value alongside its modified one. `stated` counts the distinct (module, journal `Label`) pairs a capture gives an `OriginalValue` for; `mapped` is how many name a field the record holds, split into those agreeing digit for digit and those agreeing to within the game's own float noise (it writes 20.000004 for 20, 2.499998 for 2.5, -39.999996 for -40). Nothing may disagree beyond that: a capture is Frontier's own reading, so where one contradicts a base stat the catalogue is wrong.",
    "floatNoiseTolerance": 1e-5,
    "unmappedNote": "Every label left unmapped is `DamagePerSecond`, a product of four stored stats checked in `weapons` below rather than a catalogue field of its own. Pinned as a whole list, so a label the mapping ought to resolve cannot start being skipped in silence.",
